+# Slow pantry item search
+
+For whoever investigates slow pantry item pages, including Saturday morning traffic.
+`larder/catalog.py` searches item names with Postgres full-text search and returns current stock.
+
+## Search index
+
+The repository has no database migration runner. Apply `migrations/001_catalog_search_index.sql`
+with `psql` against the application database, outside a transaction. It builds a GIN index
+concurrently so the pantry can continue serving reads and writes. The index expression matches
+the `to_tsvector('simple', name)` expression in the catalog query. Run this migration once;
+inspect any existing index with the same name before running it.
+
+Before and after applying it, capture `EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)` for representative searches:
+
+```sql
+EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)
+SELECT id, name, stock FROM pantry_items
+WHERE to_tsvector('simple', name) @@ plainto_tsquery('simple', 'rice')
+ORDER BY name;
+```
+
+Compare execution time and buffer reads using the same search terms and representative data.
+Postgres may choose a sequential scan for a small table or a common term. The index accelerates
+matching names; it does not remove sorting or database connection contention. Production timings
+are needed to establish whether it addresses the Saturday slowdown.
+
+If concurrent index creation fails, inspect `pg_index.indisvalid` for this index. An invalid index
+must be dropped before retrying. To roll back, run the following outside a transaction:
+
+```sql
+DROP INDEX CONCURRENTLY pantry_items_name_search_idx;
+```
+
+## Considering a cache
+
+Follow the [architecture rule for another service](../architecture.md#before-proposing-another-service).
+The current report names Tom as a Redis operator but does not identify a second volunteer who
+can restore it, or establish a capability Postgres cannot provide. Redis is therefore deferred
+while the existing query is indexed and measured. Any future cache design must also account for
+the stock returned by this query changing as members order items.
diff --git a/migrations/001_catalog_search_index.sql b/migrations/001_catalog_search_index.sql
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..fdce62a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/migrations/001_catalog_search_index.sql
@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
+-- Run outside a transaction so pantry reads and writes can continue.
+CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY pantry_items_name_search_idx
+    ON pantry_items USING gin (to_tsvector('simple', name));
